# Fedora Desktop - Multi-monitor setup
# Copy to outputs.conf on this machine

# Outputs are matched by identifier ("make model serial"), not connector name.
# Connector names are handed out by the GPU and shifted when the RTX 2080 went
# in: the left Acer moved DP-3 -> DP-1, so `output DP-1 disable` began switching
# off the left Acer instead of the 1080p TV, and DP-3 stopped existing entirely.
# Identifiers follow the monitor, so they survive GPU swaps and cable moves.
# Refresh after a hardware change with:
#   swaymsg -t get_outputs -r | jq -r '.[] | "\(.make) \(.model) \(.serial)"'

# Three-panel desktop layout, ordered left to right:
#   LG (1080p) | left Acer | Predator (main)
# The 4K LG is retired from this setup. Explicit positions keep the active
# desktop compact and avoid Sway placing any output at an unintended location.
# Panels are bottom-aligned on a common baseline at y=1440:
#   0 + 1920 = 1920 + 1680 = 3600 + 2560 = 6160
output "LG Electronics LG TV 0x01010101" pos 0 360 mode 1920x1080
output "Acer Technologies Acer AL2216W L92080554231" pos 1920 390 res 1680x1050
output "Acer Technologies XB271HU #ASP2u3xvGwHd" pos 3600 0 mode 2560x1440@60Hz

# The LG reports a placeholder serial; retain the full make/model/serial
# identifier so this matches only the 1080p TV.

# Workspace assignments. Keep workspaces 3/4/6 on the LG rather than letting
# them follow Sway's focused-output fallback to the Predator.
workspace 1 output "Acer Technologies XB271HU #ASP2u3xvGwHd"
workspace 2 output "Acer Technologies Acer AL2216W L92080554231"
workspace 3 output "LG Electronics LG TV 0x01010101"
workspace 4 output "LG Electronics LG TV 0x01010101"
workspace 6 output "LG Electronics LG TV 0x01010101"
